{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-43775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $E$ containing all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $\\alpha A$ where $A$ is some fixed $2\\times 2$ matrix and $\\alpha \\in R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $E$ is closed under matrix addition\n- $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $E$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- $E$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-43775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}={\\alpha }_{1}A$ and ${A}_{2}={\\alpha }_{2}A$ are two matrices from $E,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & ={\\alpha }_{1}A+{\\alpha }_{2}A=({\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{2})A,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $E.$ So, $E$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $B=\\alpha A$ is an element of $E$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kB & =k\\alpha A=(k\\alpha )A,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $E.$ So, $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $E$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-43775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46bd728db42d7a46dc8e5f34ab311f50c162c4752bf12fc437c3ccc85a69360f"} {"question" "q-43775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-43775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and IV only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III only"] ["text" "II and IV only"] ["text" "IV only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-43775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-94380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector space $C[-5,0]$ of all continuous functions $f:[-5,0]\\to R$ and its subset $B={f\\in C[-5,0]\\,|\\,f(0)=0}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $B$ is closed under function addition\n- $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $B$ is a subspace of $C[-5,0]$\n- $B$ is **not** a subspace of $C[-5,0]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-94380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is  true. If $f(x),g(x)\\in B,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(0) & =f(0)+g(0) \\\\  & =0+0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $B$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(x)\\in B$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(0) & =kf(0) \\\\  & =k\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $B$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-94380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46bd728db42d7a46dc8e5f34ab311f50c162c4752bf12fc437c3ccc85a69360f"} {"question" "q-94380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-94380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and IV only"] ["text" "I, II, and III only"] ["text" "II and IV only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "IV only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-94380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-107112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $C={[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -a\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,a\\in R}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $C$ is closed under matrix addition\n- $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $C$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- $C$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-107112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{1}\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ are two matrices from $C,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -({a}_{1}+{a}_{2})\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich is a matrix from $C.$ So, $C$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -a\\end{aligned}]$ is an element of $C$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}ka & 0 \\\\ 0 & -ka\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $C.$ So, $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $C$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-107112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46bd728db42d7a46dc8e5f34ab311f50c162c4752bf12fc437c3ccc85a69360f"} {"question" "q-107112" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-107112" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and IV only"] ["text" "I, II, and III only"] ["text" "II and IV only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "IV only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-107112" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-107113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $A={[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,a,b\\in R}.$  \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is closed under matrix addition\n- $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $A$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-107113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1} & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}]$ are two matrices from $A,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1} & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{1}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{1}+{b}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich is a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{aligned}]$ is an element of $A$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & ka \\\\ kb & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-107113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46bd728db42d7a46dc8e5f34ab311f50c162c4752bf12fc437c3ccc85a69360f"} {"question" "q-107113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-107113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and IV only"] ["text" "I, II, and III only"] ["text" "II and IV only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "IV only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-107113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-107143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $M$ containing all functions that return an integer value at $x=1.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $M$ is closed under function addition\n- $M$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $M$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n- $M$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-107143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, if $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are functions from $M,$ then $f(1)$  and  $g(1)$ are integers and so $(f+g)(1)=f(1)+g(1)$ must be an integer number too. So, $M$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, $f(x)=1$ is a function in $M$, but $0.5f(x)$ is not in $M$ because\n$(0.5f)(1)=0.5\\cdot f(1)=0.5$ is not an integer. So, $M$ is *not*  closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $M$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-107143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46bd728db42d7a46dc8e5f34ab311f50c162c4752bf12fc437c3ccc85a69360f"} {"question" "q-107143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-107143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and IV only"] ["text" "I, II, and III only"] ["text" "II and IV only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "IV only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"} {"question" "q-107143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and IV only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069368/state.json" "file_sha256" "de851f6720105693a849624ec72d5737a93e31f727cd92d5facecf921ae3b8bb"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2362 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
